From: Marcello Barnaba <vjt@openssl.it>
Subject: curl: pass --without-brotli to configure

The curl source autodetects brotli via pkg-config and links libcurl
against libbrotlidec when the headers happen to be in staging_dir, but
the OpenWrt curl Makefile has no DEPENDS entry for libbrotli — so the
post-link sanity check explodes with:

    Package libcurl is missing dependencies for the following libraries:
    libbrotlidec.so.1

We don't actually want brotli compression in libcurl on this image
(nothing on the device negotiates content-encoding: br), but our
android-tools custom feed pulls in libbrotli, which puts the headers
into staging and triggers curl's autodetect. Force --without-brotli
so curl produces a libbrotli-free libcurl regardless of staging
contents.

Upstream: not submittable as-is — the right fix is for OpenWrt's curl
Makefile to gain a CURL_BROTLI option à la CURL_ZSTD. This patch is
just enough to unbreak our image build.

--- a/feeds/packages/net/curl/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/packages/net/curl/Makefile
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@
 	--without-ca-path \
 	--without-libpsl \
 	--without-zstd \
+	--without-brotli \
 	--with-ca-bundle=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt \
 	\
 	$(call autoconf_bool,CONFIG_IPV6,ipv6) \

